# Frontend rules

## Units

- Use `rem` for layout and component sizing values instead of `px`.
- This applies to Tailwind arbitrary values and inline style values.
- Prefer token classes when available; if an arbitrary value is needed, use `rem`.

Examples:

- `size-[7.5rem]` instead of `size-[120px]`
- `max-w-[90rem]` instead of `max-w-[1440px]`
- `style={{ width: "12rem" }}` instead of `style={{ width: "192px" }}`

## Verification after frontend changes

- After making frontend code changes, always run:
  - `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`
  - `pnpm lint`
- Warnings are acceptable, but errors are not.
- If either command reports errors, fix them before considering the task complete.
